This code:

const result = await setTimeout(() => {
    return {
        success: true
    }
}, 300);

is fundamentally wrong.

setTimeout() returns:

a timer ID

NOT:

{ success: true }

So result.success becomes:

undefined

JavaScript timers are ancient chaotic browser APIs stitched together with optimism and caffeine.









